---
name: lite-qa-assignment
version: 1.0.0
description: QA assignment for the atm-bd-lite profile.
format: xml
required_variables: [task_id, phase, profile, repo, pr_number, branch, commit]
metadata:
  type: qa-assignment
  tags: [stage:qa, profile:lite]
---
<qa-task id="{{ task_id | string }}">
  <phase>{{ phase | string }}</phase>
  <profile>{{ profile | string }}</profile>
  <instructions><![CDATA[
    Review repository {{ repo }}, PR {{ pr_number }}, branch {{ branch }}, commit {{ commit }}.
    Read the task's acceptance criteria and
    verify each against the exact layer contents. Run the validation required by the task and inspect the
    stack using the installed sc-gh-stack-view skill. Always pass `--repo {{ repo }}` to GitHub PR commands;
    the primary checkout may be a different repository. An unknown local catalog is not evidence of a defect:
    verify the supplied PR base and head against the phase stack bead and report the catalog limitation.
    Report concrete evidence for every criterion.
    Close the QA task with PASS only when all criteria pass and no blocking or important findings remain;
    otherwise file findings and close with FAIL. Follow task-close T-CLOSE-03 and T-CLOSE-04.
    The task-close hook journals the bead update; never close or modify the QA bead directly.
    For FINDINGS, write a JSON array to a file, one object per finding with `id`, `title`, `description`, and
    boolean `blocking`. Then pour each finding and its required edge with this block (creating findings is allowed):

```bash
set -euo pipefail
TASK_ID='{{ task_id }}'
PHASE='{{ phase }}'
FINDINGS_FILE="${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/$TASK_ID-findings.json"
ROW=$(bd show "$TASK_ID" --json | jq -e '.[0]')
SPRINT=$(printf '%s' "$ROW" | jq -er '.metadata.sprint_bead')
ROOT=$(printf '%s' "$ROW" | jq -er '.metadata.phase_bead')
jq -ce '.[]' "$FINDINGS_FILE" | while IFS= read -r finding; do
  ID=$(printf '%s' "$finding" | jq -er '.id')
  TITLE=$(printf '%s' "$finding" | jq -er '.title')
  DESCRIPTION=$(printf '%s' "$finding" | jq -er '.description')
  BLOCKING=$(printf '%s' "$finding" | jq -er '.blocking | if type == "boolean" then tostring else error("blocking must be boolean") end')
  bd create "$TITLE" --id "$ID" --force --type bug --description "$DESCRIPTION" --labels "phase-$PHASE,stage:fix" \
    --metadata "$(jq -cn --arg sprint "$SPRINT" --arg phase "$ROOT" --argjson blocking "$BLOCKING" '{sprint_bead:$sprint,phase_bead:$phase,blocking:$blocking}')"
  if [ "$BLOCKING" = true ]; then TARGET="$SPRINT"; else TARGET="$ROOT"; fi
  bd dep add "$TARGET" --blocked-by "$ID"
done
```
    Close with an inline report ending in a single fenced JSON verdict: PASS has `verdict` and `sha`;
    FINDINGS additionally has `findings`, an array of objects containing each poured `id` and its `blocking` boolean.
    Use `atm task close {{ task_id }} completed --stdin`. If close fails, read the error, fix its named cause,
    and rerun the close; do not end your turn while your ATM task is open.
  ]]></instructions>
</qa-task>
